ser2netweb for Debian
=====================

The package installs the service ser2netweb.service but neither enables nor
starts it. It runs as the system account ser2netweb (made by systemd-sysusers),
in the group dialout for the serial ports, with its data (config.json, logs,
backups) in /var/lib/ser2netweb.

Set the first admin password, then start it now and at every boot:

  sudo -u ser2netweb ser2netweb --set-password admin
  sudo systemctl enable --now ser2netweb

Without --data-dir, the packaged ser2netweb works on /var/lib/ser2netweb, the
service's data directory ("ser2netweb --about" says "Build: distribution
package" with the distribution's name).

The web UI listens on 127.0.0.1:8080 until you choose otherwise. To reach it
from the network, add a drop-in with "sudo systemctl edit ser2netweb":

  [Service]
  Environment=SER2NETWEB_BIND_IP=0.0.0.0 SER2NETWEB_PORT=8080

Changes go into such drop-ins (/etc/systemd/system/ser2netweb.service.d/),
which an upgrade keeps. Run commands on the data directory as the account
ser2netweb, never as root (the service could not read what root writes).

pyserial-asyncio-fast is not packaged in Debian: ser2netweb then uses its
built-in copy of that library's serial transport (the start-up log and
"ser2netweb --about" say so). The recommended packages add MQTT publishing
(python3-paho-mqtt), LDAP sign-in (python3-ldap3), OpenID Connect sign-in
(python3-authlib) and self-signed certificates (python3-cryptography); each
feature says in the UI what is missing without its package.

